# proto-file: experimental/anomaly-detection/v1/generator/proto/query_template_config.proto
# proto-message: QueryTemplateConfigs
#
# Example individual (standard-user class) demonstrating Weight_Jitter
# (Requirement 17.4).
#
# weight_jitter is the lowest-precedence mechanism: a single global, non-negative
# bound. It applies to every non-pinned edge that has no variance entry with a
# positive down/up delta. For each such edge the individual's weight is perturbed
# by a value drawn uniformly from [-bound, +bound] around the class weight, drawn
# from the single seeded rng, clamped to be non-negative, then one final
# renormalization makes each node's outgoing weights sum to 1.0.
#
# No individual_edge_overrides or edge_variances are set, so the single
# weight_jitter bound governs every edge of the standard-user base graph.

markov_individual {
  base_graph_path: "../../markov_standard_user_config.textproto"

  weight_jitter {
    bound: 0.05
  }
}
